      "meaning": "You arose of old from the great ocean, and are held aloft in the sacred hand of Lord Viṣṇu. Revered and bowed down to by all the celestials, O sacred conch Pāñcajanya, salutations unto you!\n\nBy your thunderous, resonant blast resounding down to the netherworlds (pātāla), the wombs of the spouses of the demons (the enemies of the gods) are shattered into a thousand pieces. O Pāñcajanya, salutations unto you!\n\nMerely by having sight (darśana) of the conch, let alone touching it, all sins dissolve away into nothingness, just as pervasive darkness vanishes at the rising of the radiant sun!\n\nThe devotee of Viṣṇu (vaiṣṇava) who bows to the conch, touches it with their hands, recites this mantra, and bathes Lord Govinda with its sanctified water earns boundless, infinite merit (puṇya).",
